        <briefdescription>
<para>Pin TT-core pages in RAM and return an RAII bridge object. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Each TT-core for the requested vector is placed into a dedicated <computeroutput>mmap(MAP_ANONYMOUS|MAP_PRIVATE)</computeroutput> region and locked via <computeroutput>mlock()</computeroutput>. The returned <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1tensor_1_1_tensor_mmap_bridge" kindref="compound">TensorMmapBridge</ref></computeroutput> owns all regions; its destructor calls <computeroutput>munlock()</computeroutput> + <computeroutput>munmap()</computeroutput> automatically.</para>
<para>Clients should store the bridge object alive as long as any pointer from <computeroutput>bridge-&gt;slices()</computeroutput> is being used (e.g. by a GGML graph node).</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>tenant_id</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Tenant namespace. </para>
